```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
2result.sql measures the real gap of movie‑less years as `(yr − prev_yr) − 1`, then keeps only actors whose worst gap is ≤ 3.  
It also removes duplicate credits per year (`DISTINCT`), casts any year string to an integer and discards non‑positive or malformed values, so it treats entries like `'2018 '` or `'I 2009'` safely.  
0result.sql, on the other hand, keeps duplicates and filters years with a strict 4‑digit GLOB; any trailing spaces or prefixes make valid movies disappear, which can create artificial gaps.  
Therefore 2result.sql is the more accurate and resilient solution.